{"task_id":"L2-grade-co2-sufficient","layer":"L2","capability":"grade","domain":"airquality","input":{"goal":"State the indoor CO2 ppm limit and the corrective action to take when it is exceeded.","chunks":[{"text":"When indoor CO2 rises above 1000 ppm, increase the mechanical ventilation rate or open operable windows until the concentration falls back below 800 ppm. Sustained levels above 1000 ppm indicate under-ventilation relative to the current occupant load.","source":"ashrae-62.1"}]},"expected":{"sufficient":true},"judge_type":"deterministic","notes":"阈值(1000/800)+动作(增大通风)都齐→sufficient=true"}
{"task_id":"L2-grade-co2-offtopic","layer":"L2","capability":"grade","domain":"airquality","input":{"goal":"State the indoor CO2 ppm limit and the corrective action to take when it is exceeded.","chunks":[{"text":"For office spaces, ASHRAE 62.1 sets a minimum outdoor air rate of 8.5 L/s per person. Indoor CO2 concentration is an indirect indicator of whether ventilation keeps pace with occupancy, not a contaminant limit in itself.","source":"ashrae-62.1"}]},"expected":{"sufficient":false},"judge_type":"deterministic","notes":"只给 L/s 人均新风,明说 CO2 不是限值→缺 ppm 阈值+动作→false"}
{"task_id":"L2-grade-co2-missing-window","layer":"L2","capability":"grade","domain":"airquality","input":{"goal":"State the corrective ventilation action for high CO2 AND the verification stabilisation window in minutes to allow before re-checking.","chunks":[{"text":"When indoor CO2 rises above 1000 ppm, increase the mechanical ventilation rate or open operable windows until the concentration falls back below 800 ppm. Sustained levels above 1000 ppm indicate under-ventilation relative to the current occupant load.","source":"ashrae-62.1"}]},"expected":{"sufficient":false},"judge_type":"deterministic","notes":"动作有但缺‘多少分钟’的核验窗口(只 ops-note 有)→部分覆盖→false(规则2)"}
{"task_id":"L2-grade-thermal-sufficient","layer":"L2","capability":"grade","domain":"thermal","input":{"goal":"Give the operative temperature comfort range in degC for sedentary office work.","chunks":[{"text":"ASHRAE 55 defines the operative temperature comfort zone for sedentary office work as roughly 20-24 degC in winter clothing and 23-26 degC in summer clothing, assuming 50% relative humidity and low air speed.","source":"ashrae-55"}]},"expected":{"sufficient":true},"judge_type":"deterministic","notes":"舒适区范围齐全→true"}
